+/* perf(morph-close-peak v9.1): the header's panel is opacity 0 whenever .is-morphing is off (morph <= 0.001), but its
+   composited children (col-tracks, veil, center, footer) still repaint on every frame of the header's 0.68 s width
+   transition after a close. Hide them for that window only: a one-shot visibility keyframe on the panel's children
+   (not on the panel: it is a scene element whose animations the scene engine pauses). At rest they are visible again,
+   as before: a hidden, paused col-track animation made Chrome request a main frame every vsync (v9 int census). */
+@keyframes fw-morph-close-hide {
+  0%,
+  100% {
+    visibility: hidden;
+  }
+}
